{"type":"text","timestamp":1787403915989,"sessionID":"ses_fd66e2edfffeGpQNrzP0HLTiRE","part":{"id":"prt_029934cbb001sdWl5yyDI5cYeI","messageID":"msg_029934152001r0MGCDDFw3G0dA","sessionID":"ses_fd66e2edfffeGpQNrzP0HLTiRE","type":"text","text":"All three helpers are reimplemented per contract. Summary of changes to `lib/utils.js`:\n\n- **`basename(path, { windows })`** — splits on `/` always, and `\\\\` only when `windows` is set; returns the last non-empty segment (so a trailing separator is skipped).\n- **`escapeLast(input, char, lastIdx)`** — escapes the last `char` at/before `lastIdx`, recursing leftwards when the occurrence is already escaped.\n- **`removePrefix(input, state = {})`** — strips a single leading `./`, records `state.prefix = './'`, leaves `state` untouched otherwise, and works when `state` is omitted.\n\nLocal check: the existing test suite shows 3 pass / 5 fail, identical to the pre-change baseline — so no regressions were introduced. The 5 failures are pre-existing in this repo.","time":{"start":1787403914427,"end":1787403915986}}}
